IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa10-types`
IMPORT `coa10-period`
IMPORT `coa10-filing`

-- coa10-exemptions.l4: Chapter 10, ss 448 to 448C of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom): unlimited companies and
-- dormant subsidiaries exempt from the obligation to file accounts, the companies excluded from the dormant subsidiaries
-- exemption, and the parent undertaking's guarantee. Lines 6060-6117 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is
-- within the rule; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the words>"`); NOTHING = the text does not decide
-- (each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 448: unlimited companies exempt from obligation to file accounts
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "limited at a particular time": an undertaking (under whatever law established) the liability of whose members is at that time limited.
-- src:6066 | The references above to an undertaking being limited at a particular time are to an undertaking (under whatever law established) the liability of whose members is at that time limited.
@ref s 448(2) "limited" at a particular time (src:6066)
GIVEN `the liability of the undertaking's members is limited at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(2) the undertaking was limited at that time` MEANS
    IF `the liability of the undertaking's members is limited at that time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are to an undertaking (under whatever law established) the liability of whose members is at that time limited"

-- src:6062 | (2) The conditions are that at no time during the relevant accounting reference period—
-- src:6063 | (a) has the company been, to its knowledge, a subsidiary undertaking of an undertaking which was then limited, or
@ref s 448(2)(a) At no time has the company been, to its knowledge, a subsidiary undertaking of a limited undertaking (src:6062-6063)
GIVEN `at some time during the relevant accounting reference period the company has been, to its knowledge, a subsidiary undertaking of an undertaking which was then limited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(2)(a) the condition is met` MEANS
    IF `at some time during the relevant accounting reference period the company has been, to its knowledge, a subsidiary undertaking of an undertaking which was then limited`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are that at no time during the relevant accounting reference period— (a) has the company been, to its knowledge, a subsidiary undertaking of an undertaking which was then limited"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:6062 | (2) The conditions are that at no time during the relevant accounting reference period—
-- src:6064 | (b) have there been, to its knowledge, exercisable by or on behalf of two or more undertakings which were then limited, rights which if exercisable by one of them would have made the company a subsidiary undertaking of it, or
@ref s 448(2)(b) At no time have rights been exercisable by two or more limited undertakings that would have made the company a subsidiary undertaking (src:6062 and src:6064)
GIVEN `at some time during the relevant accounting reference period there have been, to its knowledge, exercisable by or on behalf of two or more undertakings which were then limited, rights which if exercisable by one of them would have made the company a subsidiary undertaking of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(2)(b) the condition is met` MEANS
    IF `at some time during the relevant accounting reference period there have been, to its knowledge, exercisable by or on behalf of two or more undertakings which were then limited, rights which if exercisable by one of them would have made the company a subsidiary undertaking of it`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) have there been, to its knowledge, exercisable by or on behalf of two or more undertakings which were then limited, rights which if exercisable by one of them would have made the company a subsidiary undertaking of it"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:6062 | (2) The conditions are that at no time during the relevant accounting reference period—
-- src:6065 | (c) has the company been a parent company of an undertaking which was then limited.
@ref s 448(2)(c) At no time has the company been a parent company of a limited undertaking (src:6062 and src:6065)
GIVEN `at some time during the relevant accounting reference period the company has been a parent company of an undertaking which was then limited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(2)(c) the condition is met` MEANS
    IF `at some time during the relevant accounting reference period the company has been a parent company of an undertaking which was then limited`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) has the company been a parent company of an undertaking which was then limited"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:6061 | (1) The directors of an unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports to the registrar in respect of a financial year if the following conditions are met.
-- src:6062 | (2) The conditions are that at no time during the relevant accounting reference period—
-- src:6063 | (a) has the company been, to its knowledge, a subsidiary undertaking of an undertaking which was then limited, or
-- src:6064 | (b) have there been, to its knowledge, exercisable by or on behalf of two or more undertakings which were then limited, rights which if exercisable by one of them would have made the company a subsidiary undertaking of it, or
-- src:6065 | (c) has the company been a parent company of an undertaking which was then limited.
@ref s 448(2) The three conditions together (src:6061-6065)
GIVEN `the condition in paragraph (a) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (b) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the condition in paragraph (c) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(2) the conditions are met` MEANS
    `s 441 both are true` (`s 441 both are true` `the condition in paragraph (a) is met` `the condition in paragraph (b) is met`) `the condition in paragraph (c) is met`

-- s 448(3)(a): a banking or insurance company, or the parent of a banking or insurance group (the keel's answers, BOOLEAN suffices).
-- src:6068 | (a) the company is a banking or insurance company or the parent company of a banking or insurance group, or
@ref s 448(3)(a) A banking or insurance company, or the parent company of a banking or insurance group (src:6068)
GIVEN `s 1164(2) the company is a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1165(3) the company is an insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1164(4) the company is the parent company of a banking group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1165(5) the company is the parent company of an insurance group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 448(3)(a) the company is a banking or insurance company or the parent company of a banking or insurance group` MEANS
    `s 1164(2) the company is a banking company` OR `s 1165(3) the company is an insurance company` OR `s 1164(4) the company is the parent company of a banking group` OR `s 1165(5) the company is the parent company of an insurance group`

-- s 448(3)(b): each member is (i) a limited company, (ii) another unlimited company each of whose members is a limited company,
-- (iii) a Scottish partnership that is not a limited partnership, each of whose members is a limited company, or (iv) a Scottish
-- limited partnership, each of whose general partners is a limited company. The kind a member is comes from the caller.
-- src:6069 | (b) each of the members of the company is—
-- src:6070 | (i) a limited company,
-- src:6071 | (ii) another unlimited company each of whose members is a limited company, . . .
-- src:6072 | (iii) a Scottish partnership which is not a limited partnership, each of whose members is a limited company , or
-- src:6073 | (iv) a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership, each of whose general partners is a limited company.
@ref s 448(3)(b)(i)-(iv) The kinds of member that take the company out of the exemption (src:6069-6073)
DECLARE `s 448 kind of member` IS ONE OF
    `s 448 a limited company`
    `s 448 another unlimited company each of whose members is a limited company`
    `s 448 a Scottish partnership which is not a limited partnership, each of whose members is a limited company`
    `s 448 a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership, each of whose general partners is a limited company`
    `s 448 any other kind of member`

-- src:6069 | (b) each of the members of the company is—
-- src:6070 | (i) a limited company,
-- src:6071 | (ii) another unlimited company each of whose members is a limited company, . . .
-- src:6072 | (iii) a Scottish partnership which is not a limited partnership, each of whose members is a limited company , or
-- src:6073 | (iv) a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership, each of whose general partners is a limited company.
@ref s 448(3)(b) Each of the members of the company is one of those kinds (src:6069-6073)
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `s 448 kind of member`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(3)(b) each of the members of the company is of a kind that paragraph (b) names` MEANS
    IF null members
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what "each of the members" means for a company with none
    ELSE IF all (GIVEN m YIELD NOT (m EQUALS `s 448 any other kind of member`)) members
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "if" not met): "does not apply if— ... (b) each of the members of the company is— (i) a limited company ..."

-- The last sentence of (3): the references include a comparable undertaking incorporated outside the United Kingdom.
-- src:6074 | The references in paragraph (b) to a limited company, another unlimited company , a Scottish partnership which is not a limited partnership or a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership include a comparable undertaking incorporated in or formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom.
@ref s 448(3) The references include a comparable undertaking incorporated outside the United Kingdom (src:6074)
GIVEN `the undertaking is incorporated in or formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is comparable to the kind of member that paragraph (b) names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(3) the undertaking counts as a member of a kind that paragraph (b) names` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is incorporated in or formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` AND `the undertaking is comparable to the kind of member that paragraph (b) names`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include a comparable undertaking incorporated in or formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom"

-- s 448(3): the sentence that takes the company out of the exemption. Title as the bar: JUST TRUE means the exemption does not apply.
-- src:6067 | (3) The exemption conferred by this section does not apply if—
-- src:6068 | (a) the company is a banking or insurance company or the parent company of a banking or insurance group, or
-- src:6069 | (b) each of the members of the company is—
-- src:6070 | (i) a limited company,
-- src:6071 | (ii) another unlimited company each of whose members is a limited company, . . .
-- src:6072 | (iii) a Scottish partnership which is not a limited partnership, each of whose members is a limited company , or
-- src:6073 | (iv) a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership, each of whose general partners is a limited company.
-- src:6074 | The references in paragraph (b) to a limited company, another unlimited company , a Scottish partnership which is not a limited partnership or a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership include a comparable undertaking incorporated in or formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom.
@ref s 448(3) The exemption does not apply to a banking or insurance company, or where each member is limited (src:6067-6074)
GIVEN `paragraph (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b) holds` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(3) the section bars the exemption` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (a) holds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `paragraph (b) holds`

-- src:6060 | 448 Unlimited companies exempt from obligation to file accounts
-- src:6061 | (1) The directors of an unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports to the registrar in respect of a financial year if the following conditions are met.
-- src:6067 | (3) The exemption conferred by this section does not apply if—
@ref s 448(1) The directors of an unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports (src:6060-6061 and src:6067)
GIVEN `the company is an unlimited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 448(2) the conditions are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 448(3) the section bars the exemption` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(1) the directors of the unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is an unlimited company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directors of an unlimited company"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 448(3) the section bars the exemption`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The exemption conferred by this section does not apply if"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
             CONSIDER `s 448(2) the conditions are met`
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "if" not met): "are not required to deliver accounts and reports in respect of a financial year if the following conditions are met"
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             CONSIDER `s 448(2) the conditions are met`
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "if" not met): "are not required to deliver accounts and reports in respect of a financial year if the following conditions are met"
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the exemption is barred by subsection (3) is not known
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): neither answer is known

-- s 448(4): where the company is exempt by virtue of the section, ss 434(3) and 435(1)(b) have effect with a substitution.
-- src:6075 | (4) Where a company is exempt by virtue of this section from the obligation to deliver accounts—
-- src:6076 | (a) section 434(3) (requirements in connection with publication of statutory accounts: meaning of “statutory accounts”) has effect with the substitution for the words “as required to be delivered to the registrar under section 441” of the words “as prepared in accordance with this Part and approved by the board of directors”; and
@ref s 448(4)(a) Section 434(3) has effect with a substitution (src:6075-6076)
GIVEN `s 448(1) the directors of the unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 448(4)(a) the words substituted in section 434(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 448(1) the directors of the unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST "as prepared in accordance with this Part and approved by the board of directors"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company is exempt by virtue of this section from the obligation to deliver accounts"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is exempt is not known

-- src:6075 | (4) Where a company is exempt by virtue of this section from the obligation to deliver accounts—
-- src:6077 | (b) section 435(1)(b) (requirements in connection with publication of non-statutory accounts: statement whether statutory accounts delivered) has effect with the substitution for the words from “whether statutory accounts” to “have been delivered to the registrar” of the words “that the company is exempt from the requirement to deliver statutory accounts”.
@ref s 448(4)(b) Section 435(1)(b) has effect with a substitution (src:6075 and src:6077)
GIVEN `s 448(1) the directors of the unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 448(4)(b) the words substituted in section 435(1)(b)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 448(1) the directors of the unlimited company are not required to deliver accounts and reports`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST "that the company is exempt from the requirement to deliver statutory accounts"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company is exempt by virtue of this section from the obligation to deliver accounts"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is exempt is not known

-- s 448(5): "general partner", "limited partnership" (Limited Partnerships Act 1907, borrowed facts) and "relevant accounting reference period".
-- src:6079 | “ general partner ” means—
-- src:6080 | (a) in relation to a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership, a person who is a general partner within the meaning of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 ; and
-- src:6081 | (b) in relation to an undertaking incorporated in or formed under the law of any country or territory outside the United Kingdom and which is comparable to a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership, a person comparable to such a general partner;
@ref s 448(5) "general partner" (src:6079-6081)
GIVEN `the person is a general partner within the meaning of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 of a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person comparable to such a general partner in an undertaking incorporated in or formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom that is comparable to a Scottish limited partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(5) the person is a general partner` MEANS
    IF `the person is a general partner within the meaning of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 of a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership` OR `the person is a person comparable to such a general partner in an undertaking incorporated in or formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom that is comparable to a Scottish limited partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“general partner” means— (a) in relation to a Scottish partnership which is a limited partnership, a person who is a general partner within the meaning of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907; and (b) ..."

-- src:6082 | “ limited partnership ” means a partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907; and the “ relevant accounting reference period ”, in relation to a financial year, means the accounting reference period by reference to which that financial year was determined.
@ref s 448(5) "limited partnership" (src:6082)
GIVEN `the partnership is registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(5) the partnership is a limited partnership` MEANS
    IF `the partnership is registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“limited partnership” means a partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907"

-- src:6082 | “ limited partnership ” means a partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907; and the “ relevant accounting reference period ”, in relation to a financial year, means the accounting reference period by reference to which that financial year was determined.
@ref s 448(5) "relevant accounting reference period" (src:6082)
GIVEN `the financial year was determined by reference to the accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448(5) the accounting reference period is the relevant accounting reference period in relation to the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the financial year was determined by reference to the accounting reference period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the “relevant accounting reference period”, in relation to a financial year, means the accounting reference period by reference to which that financial year was determined"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 448B: companies excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The text shows paragraphs (b) and (c) only: the lead-in and paragraph (a) are absent from the file, and the heading is
-- "Companies excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption". A company within (b) or (c) is excluded (JUST TRUE); the
-- list cannot be taken as closed, so a company within neither is NOTHING (fork F9 in NOTES.md).
-- src:6101 | 448B Companies excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption
-- src:6102 | (b) a company that—
-- src:6103 | (i) is an authorised insurance company, a banking company, an e-Money issuer, a MiFID investment firm or a UCITS management company, or
-- src:6104 | (ii) carries on insurance market activity, or
-- src:6105 | (c) a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (c 52) or an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992 ( S.I. 1992/807) ( NI 5).
@ref s 448B Companies excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption (src:6101-6105)
GIVEN `s 1165(2) the company is an authorised insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1164(2) the company is a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 474(1) the company is an e-money issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 474(1) the company is a MiFID investment firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 474(1) the company is a UCITS management company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1165 the company carries on insurance market activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448B the company is excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption` MEANS
    LET `paragraph (b)(i)` MEANS
                `s 1165(2) the company is an authorised insurance company`
             OR `s 1164(2) the company is a banking company`
             OR `s 474(1) the company is an e-money issuer`
             OR `s 474(1) the company is a MiFID investment firm`
             OR `s 474(1) the company is a UCITS management company`
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
            `s 441 either is true`
                `the company is a special register body as defined in section 117(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992`
                `the company is an employers' association as defined in section 122 of that Act or Article 4 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992`
    IN IF `paragraph (b)(i)` OR `s 1165 the company carries on insurance market activity`
       THEN JUST TRUE
       ELSE CONSIDER `paragraph (c)`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the lead-in and paragraph (a) are absent from this text, so the list of excluded companies cannot be taken as closed
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 definitions are not among the sources

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 448C: parent undertaking declaration of guarantee
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6107 | (1) A guarantee is given by a parent undertaking under this section when the directors of the subsidiary company deliver to the registrar a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company under this section.
@ref s 448C(1) A guarantee is given when the directors of the subsidiary deliver the parent's statement (src:6107)
GIVEN `the directors of the subsidiary company have delivered to the registrar a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company under section 448C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the directors of the subsidiary company have delivered to the registrar a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company under section 448C`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "when" read as a "where", ruling of 2026-11-05): "A guarantee is given by a parent undertaking under this section when the directors of the subsidiary company deliver to the registrar a statement by the parent undertaking that it guarantees the subsidiary company"

-- (2)(c) is blank in this text (a row of dots), so the five items are (a), (b), (d), (e) and (f).
-- src:6108 | (2) The statement under subsection (1) must be authenticated by the parent undertaking and must specify—
-- src:6109 | (a) the name of the parent undertaking,
-- src:6110 | (b) the registered number (if any) of the parent undertaking,
-- src:6112 | (d) the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given,
-- src:6113 | (e) the date of the statement, and
-- src:6114 | (f) the financial year to which the guarantee relates.
@ref s 448C(2) The statement must be authenticated and must specify (src:6108-6110 and src:6112-6114)
GIVEN `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement specifies the name of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement specifies the registered number (if any) of the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement specifies the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement specifies the date of the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement specifies the financial year to which the guarantee relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448C(2) the statement meets the requirements of the section` MEANS
    IF     `the statement is authenticated by the parent undertaking`
       AND `the statement specifies the name of the parent undertaking`
       AND `the statement specifies the registered number (if any) of the parent undertaking`
       AND `the statement specifies the name and registered number of the subsidiary company in respect of which the guarantee is being given`
       AND `the statement specifies the date of the statement`
       AND `the statement specifies the financial year to which the guarantee relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not done, decided at this site, ruling of 2026-11-05): "The statement under subsection (1) must be authenticated by the parent undertaking and must specify"

-- src:6115 | (3) A guarantee given under this section has the effect that—
-- src:6116 | (a) the parent undertaking guarantees all outstanding liabilities to which the subsidiary company is subject at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates, until they are satisfied in full, and
@ref s 448C(3)(a) The parent undertaking guarantees all outstanding liabilities until they are satisfied in full (src:6115-6116)
GIVEN `s 448C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the liabilities to which the subsidiary company is subject at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of those liabilities that has been satisfied (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 448C(3)(a) the amount of the outstanding liabilities that the parent undertaking still guarantees` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 448C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (max 0 (`the liabilities to which the subsidiary company is subject at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates (in pounds)` MINUS `the amount of those liabilities that has been satisfied (in pounds)`))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A guarantee given under this section has the effect that"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a guarantee is given is not known

-- src:6115 | (3) A guarantee given under this section has the effect that—
-- src:6117 | (b) the guarantee is enforceable against the parent undertaking by any person to whom the subsidiary company is liable in respect of those liabilities.
@ref s 448C(3)(b) The guarantee is enforceable against the parent undertaking by any person to whom the subsidiary company is liable (src:6115 and src:6117)
GIVEN `s 448C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary company is liable to the person in respect of liabilities outstanding at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448C(3)(b) the person may enforce the guarantee against the parent undertaking` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 448C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the subsidiary company is liable to the person in respect of liabilities outstanding at the end of the financial year to which the guarantee relates`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by any person to whom the subsidiary company is liable in respect of those liabilities"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A guarantee given under this section has the effect that"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a guarantee is given is not known

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 448A: dormant subsidiaries exempt from obligation to file accounts
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (2)(c): included in the consolidated accounts the parent undertaking draws up for that year, or to an earlier date in that year.
-- src:6091 | (c) the company must be included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking in accordance with—
-- src:6092 | (i) if the undertaking is a company, the requirements of this Part of this Act, or, if the undertaking is not a company, the legal requirements which apply to the drawing up of consolidated accounts for that undertaking, or
-- src:6093 | (ii) UK-adopted international accounting standards,
@ref s 448A(2)(c) The company is included in the consolidated accounts the parent undertaking draws up (src:6091-6093)
GIVEN `the company is included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are drawn up in accordance with the requirements of this Part (if the parent undertaking is a company) or the legal requirements that apply to the drawing up of consolidated accounts for that undertaking (if it is not)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are drawn up in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448A(2)(c) the company is included in consolidated accounts drawn up as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the company is included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking`
       AND (`they are drawn up in accordance with the requirements of this Part (if the parent undertaking is a company) or the legal requirements that apply to the drawing up of consolidated accounts for that undertaking (if it is not)` OR `they are drawn up in accordance with UK-adopted international accounting standards`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not done, decided at this site, ruling of 2026-11-05): "the company must be included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking in accordance with"

-- (2)(e): the directors must deliver five documents within the period for filing. Days are counted from the end of the
-- financial year's accounting reference period, as in s 442 (the deadline is the number of days to the end of the period for filing).
-- src:6095 | (e) the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar within the period for filing the company's accounts and reports for that year—
-- src:6096 | (i) a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a),
-- src:6097 | (ii) the statement referred to in section 448C(1),
-- src:6098 | (iii) a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c),
-- src:6099 | (iv) a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts, and
-- src:6100 | (v) a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking.
@ref s 448A(2)(e) The directors must deliver five documents within the period for filing (src:6095-6100)
GIVEN `a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a) has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement referred to in section 448C(1) has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c) has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the day the last of them was delivered` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448A(2)(e) the directors have delivered the documents within the period for filing` MEANS
    IF     `a written notice of the agreement referred to in subsection (2)(a) has been delivered`
       AND `the statement referred to in section 448C(1) has been delivered`
       AND `a copy of the consolidated accounts referred to in subsection (2)(c) has been delivered`
       AND `a copy of the auditor's report on those accounts has been delivered`
       AND `a copy of the consolidated annual report drawn up by the parent undertaking has been delivered`
       AND `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the day the last of them was delivered` AT MOST `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not done, and a period fixed in the text's own words, rulings of 2026-11-05): "the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar within the period for filing the company's accounts and reports for that year"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: the directors of the dormant subsidiary deliver within the period for filing.
-- src:6095 | (e) the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar within the period for filing the company's accounts and reports for that year—
@ref s 448A(2)(e) The directors must deliver within the period for filing (a regulative rule) (src:6095)
GIVEN `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 448A(2)(e) the directors' duty to deliver the documents` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Director, Registrar, "deliver a written notice of the agreement, the statement under section 448C(1), a copy of the consolidated accounts, a copy of the auditor's report on them and a copy of the consolidated annual report"
    WITHIN `the number of days from the end of the accounting reference period to the end of the period for filing` -- days, counted from the end of the accounting reference period
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "s 448A(2)(e): the documents were not delivered within the period for filing, so the exemption is not complied with"

-- src:6088 | (2) Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions—
-- src:6089 | (a) all members of the company must agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year in question,
-- src:6090 | (b) the parent undertaking must give a guarantee under section 448C in respect of that year,
-- src:6091 | (c) the company must be included in the consolidated accounts drawn up for that year or to an earlier date in that year by the parent undertaking in accordance with—
-- src:6092 | (i) if the undertaking is a company, the requirements of this Part of this Act, or, if the undertaking is not a company, the legal requirements which apply to the drawing up of consolidated accounts for that undertaking, or
-- src:6093 | (ii) UK-adopted international accounting standards,
-- src:6094 | (d) the parent undertaking must disclose in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the directors of the company are exempt from the requirement to deliver a copy of the company's individual accounts to the registrar by virtue of this section, and
-- src:6095 | (e) the directors of the company must deliver to the registrar within the period for filing the company's accounts and reports for that year—
@ref s 448A(2) Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all five conditions (src:6088-6095)
GIVEN `all the members of the company agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 448C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 448A(2)(c) the company is included in consolidated accounts drawn up as the paragraph requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the parent undertaking discloses in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the directors of the company are exempt from the requirement to deliver a copy of the company's individual accounts to the registrar by virtue of section 448A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 448A(2)(e) the directors have delivered the documents within the period for filing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448A(2) the conditions for the exemption are complied with` MEANS
    LET `paragraph (a)` MEANS JUST `all the members of the company agree to the exemption in respect of the financial year in question`
        `paragraph (d)` MEANS JUST `the parent undertaking discloses in the notes to the consolidated accounts that the directors of the company are exempt from the requirement to deliver a copy of the company's individual accounts to the registrar by virtue of section 448A`
    IN `s 441 both are true`
           (`s 441 both are true`
                (`s 441 both are true` `paragraph (a)` `s 448C(1) a guarantee is given by the parent undertaking`)
                (`s 441 both are true` `s 448A(2)(c) the company is included in consolidated accounts drawn up as the paragraph requires` `paragraph (d)`))
           `s 448A(2)(e) the directors have delivered the documents within the period for filing`

-- src:6084 | (1) The directors of a company are not required to deliver a copy of the company's individual accounts to the registrar in respect of a financial year if—
-- src:6085 | (a) the company is a subsidiary undertaking,
-- src:6086 | (b) it has been dormant throughout the whole of that year, and
-- src:6087 | (c) its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 448A(1) The directors of a dormant subsidiary are not required to deliver a copy of the individual accounts (src:6084-6087)
GIVEN `the company is a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1169(1) the company has been dormant throughout the whole of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 448A(2) the conditions for the exemption are complied with` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 448B the company is excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 448A(1) the directors of the dormant subsidiary are not required to deliver a copy of the individual accounts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is a subsidiary undertaking` AND `s 1169(1) the company has been dormant throughout the whole of the financial year` AND `the company's parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "if" not met): "are not required to deliver a copy of the company's individual accounts to the registrar in respect of a financial year if— (a) the company is a subsidiary undertaking, (b) it has been dormant throughout the whole of that year, and (c) its parent undertaking is established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 448B the company is excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, the heading of s 448B): "Companies excluded from the dormant subsidiaries exemption"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 448A(2) the conditions for the exemption are complied with`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             CONSIDER `s 448A(2) the conditions for the exemption are complied with`
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Exemption is conditional upon compliance with all of the following conditions"
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 448B's lead-in and paragraph (a) are absent, so a company within neither (b) nor (c) is not shown to be outside the exclusion
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answers the exemption needs are not known
